# Story 8: Sending Input Remotely (45s)
# Hook: Drive a session from the outside -- no attach required.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-008-sending-input-remotely.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 5

[00:00.0 --> 00:05.0]
Drive a running session from the outside -- no attach required.

[00:05.0 --> 00:15.0]
rysh send delivers input to a session's active pane. Here we run ls -la in my-session without attaching.

[00:15.0 --> 00:24.0]
Add --pane with a pane ID to target one exact pane.

[00:24.0 --> 00:34.0]
Use --mode prompt to send an AI prompt instead of a command -- the agent in that pane handles it.

[00:34.0 --> 00:45.0]
Or --mode shell to run a command explicitly. Omit --mode and Rysh uses the pane's current mode.

